    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #161\n\n- 2026-09-12 13:43Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-12 14:22Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #392 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-161-realtime-v1-02-06-bridge-transactional-thr_8dknkdktf3` to origin. ## Summary This implements issue #161: standardizing transactional NOTIFY on the `semprec_events` channel and bridging it to WebSocket clients. **Key changes:** - All choke-point writes (items, databases, properties, views) fire a thin `notifyInvalidation` event via `runAfterCommit` — never before commit, never on rollback — carrying only `scope`/`databaseId`/`itemId`/`op`/`updatedAt`, never full row content. - Document writes emit `docId`/`updateId`; notification commits emit `userId`/`notificationId` — no raw Yjs updates or pre-rendered notification content travel over NOTIFY. - The `WS /api/sync` sync server (from issue #160) now fans out: item/schema invalidations broadcast as thin references to every connected socket (Semprec is a one-/two-user system, so no per-row filtering), while notifications fetch the full current row via `getNotificationById` and deliver it only to sockets authenticated as that notification's own user. - Rollup and journal-inbox recompute re-fetch `updatedAt` after `writeComputed` (which doesn't bump it) before announcing an invalidation. - Deleted `wsServer.ts`, a previously-unmounted duplicate broadcast mechanism (confirmed dead code by reading `serve.ts`), and ported its proven broadcast/user-scoping logic into `syncServer.ts` instead. **Verification:** `backend/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 93 test files / 1127 tests, e2e) and `web/pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 139 tests) both pass in full. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 15:17Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #392 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed commit `ec43c8c` to branch `bb/relay-161-realtime-v1-02-06-bridge-transactional-thr_8dknkdktf3` (same branch as the earlier push, updating existing PR #392). ## Summary Implements issue #161 — bridging transactional invalidations and notifications through PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY — and addresses the code-review feedback received on PR #392: - **User-scoped invalidation delivery**: `chokePoint.ts`'s ~13 REST-reachable write methods (`createItem`, `updateItem`, `softDeleteItem`, `restoreItem`, `createDatabase`, `renameDatabase`, `archiveDatabase`, `createProperty`, `updateProperty`, `deleteProperty`, `createView`, `patchView`, `deleteView`) now accept an optional `actingUserId`, sourced from `ctx.identity.user.id` in the REST handlers. `syncServer.ts` delivers the resulting invalidation frame only to that user's own sockets (`sendToUser`), falling back to broadcast only for system/background writes that have no single acting user (rollup recompute, mail sync, etc.) — this satisfies the acceptance criterion that cross-user delivery is impossible for REST-driven writes. - **Runtime validation at the NOTIFY boundary**: replaced an unchecked `as RealtimeMessage` cast with `parseRealtimeMessage`, a full validator covering the closed `RealtimeMessage` catalog. - **New ADR** (`docs/adr/2026-09-12-thin-user-scoped-realtime-invalidations.md`) documenting both the thin-payload rule and the new user-scoped-fanout rule, including the rationale for the background-write broadcast fallback. - **Test coverage**: updated `syncServer.test.ts` to prove scoped delivery to the acting user only, prove the fallback-broadcast path for system writes, and add a new test proving a missed invalidation is never replayed to a reconnecting socket. Both `backend` and `web` full `pnpm run verify` pipelines pass (lint, format, build, unit/integration/e2e tests, migration and boundary checks). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 15:49Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #392 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed commit `915e6d5` to branch `bb/relay-161-realtime-v1-02-06-bridge-transactional-thr_8dknkdktf3` (same branch as before, updating existing PR #392). ## Summary Implements issue #161 — bridging transactional invalidations and notifications through PostgreSQL LISTEN/NOTIFY — and addresses two rounds of code-review feedback on PR #392: **First round:** - User-scoped invalidation delivery: `chokePoint.ts`'s ~13 REST-reachable write methods now accept an optional `actingUserId` (sourced from `ctx.identity.user.id`); `syncServer.ts` delivers item/schema invalidation frames only to that user's own sockets, falling back to broadcast only for writes with no single acting user (background/system jobs). - Runtime validation (`parseRealtimeMessage`) at the NOTIFY boundary, replacing an unchecked type cast. - New ADR documenting the thin-payload and user-scoped-fanout rules. - Test coverage proving scoped delivery, the broadcast fallback, and that a missed invalidation is never replayed on reconnect. **Second round:** - Fixed a medium-severity cross-user delivery risk: `forwardNotification` now re-verifies the fetched notification row's own `userId` against the NOTIFY payload's claimed `userId` before sending, rather than trusting the payload outright. - Documented and tested the reconnect-heal protocol for AC #11: active views/open items heal via their normal REST endpoints, unread notifications heal via the existing `GET /api/notifications/unread` endpoint (issue #36/#152) — the same endpoint a client already calls on first connect. Added a test proving a notification missed while disconnected is never replayed, with the still-unread row confirmed available for the client's own refetch. Both `backend` and `web` full `pnpm run verify` pipelines pass (backend: 1374 tests total across unit/integration/e2e tiers; web: 139 tests), including lint, format, build, and migration/boundary checks. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 16:08Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #392 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 All three commits (including this turn's fixes) are already merged into `develop` via PR #392, which merged as `daf56d8`. The branch push just re-created the now-deleted branch ref at the already-merged SHA — no new work, nothing outstanding. Issue #161 is fully shipped. Branch: `bb/relay-161-realtime-v1-02-06-bridge-transactional-thr_8dknkdktf3` (pushed to origin, matching the commits already merged into `develop` via PR #392). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-12 16:08Z — This issue was resolved by #392, which just merged into develop.",
